        "original_id": "44913384-06d1-57bf-bfd4-d89df2ee5a88",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Salvia, Arachis\n- Families and clades: Lamiaceae, Fabaceae, Dalbergieae, Pterocarpus clade\n- Concepts: plant genera, species counts, native range\n\nFacts:\n- Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the mint family Lamiaceae.\n- Salvia includes nearly 1000 species of shrubs, herbaceous perennials, and annuals.\n- Arachis is a genus of about 70 species of annual and perennial flowering plants in the pea family Fabaceae.\n- Arachis is native to South America.\n- Arachis was recently assigned to the informal monophyletic Pterocarpus clade of the tribe Dalbergieae.",
